course: dictionary
lesson: 11764
title: Barnacle
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A barnacle is a small sea animal with a hard shell. It sticks itself onto rocks, ships and even whales, and it stays there. Context helps here: «The old boat was covered in barnacles» tells you they grow on things in the sea.
explain: Barnacles are related to crabs. They catch their food by waving their feathery legs in the water. Think about where you would find one: on a beach, on a pier, or in a rock pool.
explain: The word has a second meaning too. «My cousin is a barnacle; he follows me everywhere and will not go away.» Here a barnacle is a person who sticks to someone, just like the animal sticks to a rock. Check by swapping in your meaning: "He is a person who sticks to me and will not leave" still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: A barnacle is a small sea animal with a hard shell.
fact: «Barnacle» means a small sea animal that sticks to rocks, ships and whales and stays there.
fact: Barnacles are related to crabs, and they feed by waving their feathery legs.
fact: Informal: «barnacle» can also mean a person who sticks to someone and will not go away.
fact: Phrases you may hear: «covered in barnacles» and «barnacle geese».
exercise: «The old boat was covered in barnacles.» What are barnacles? | Fish that swim very fast through the waves | Pieces of wood that float from a ship | *Small sea animals with hard shells | Seaweed that grows on the sand
exercise: «Our rock pool was full of crabs and barnacles.» Barnacles are related to which animal? | *Crabs | Starfish | Seagulls | Jellyfish
exercise: Sam says, «My little sister follows me everywhere and will not go away. She is a real barnacle!» What does barnacle mean here? | *A person who sticks to someone and will not go away | A type of ship that sails the sea | A small crab that lives in rock pools | A bird that flies over the waves
test: How do barnacles catch their food? | By digging holes in the sand | By floating on the top of the water | By chasing fish with sharp teeth | *By waving their feathery legs in the water
test: Which sentence uses barnacle in the informal way? | «The barnacles on the pier were green and slimy.» | «The barnacle geese flew over the sea.» | *«My brother is a barnacle; he will not leave me alone.» | «The ship sailed out of the harbour.»
exam: Which of these is a small sea animal that sticks to rocks and ships? | Seagull | Shark | Dolphin | *Barnacle
